# Copy this file to `.env` for local overrides (`.env` is gitignored, this
# example file is not — see `frontend/.gitignore`).
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed `VITE_`, and only reads them at BUILD
# time: `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` is replaced with a literal string
# inside the bundled JS while `vite build` runs. Setting/changing this
# environment variable on Netlify AFTER the site was already built does
# nothing until the next build/deploy — it is not read again at request time
# in the browser.
#
# Locally, leaving this unset falls back to http://127.0.0.1:8000 (see
# `frontend/src/api.ts`), which matches `python -m uvicorn app.main:app --port
# 8000` from `backend/`.
#
# In Netlify's site settings (Site configuration -> Environment variables),
# set this to the deployed Hugging Face Space's URL, in the form
# https://<hf-username>-<space-name>.hf.space (no trailing slash needed —
# `api.ts` strips one if present).
VITE_API_URL=https://<hf-username>-<space-name>.hf.space
